\vspace{-2pt}
\paragraph{Environment complexity boundary.}
\looseness=-1 Cross-environment analysis across six DMC tasks (1--21 DoF; Table~\ref{tab:cross_env_civo}) reveals that CIVO occupies a complexity Goldilocks zone: 1-DoF (Cartpole, 0/3) and 4-DoF (Hopper, 0/1) never trigger onset, while 12-DoF (Quadruped) and 21-DoF (Humanoid) baselines exhibit intrinsic value overestimation (NVE $4.7\times$ and $12.97\times$ without the gate mechanism) that precludes CIVO isolation. Onset occurs exclusively at 6 DoF (Walker 60\%, Cheetah 75\%), suggesting CIVO requires sufficient dynamic complexity for temporal embeddings to develop exploitable value bias, yet a stable baseline where gate-induced perturbation dominates. For transformer-based world models \citep{micheli2023iris}, whether this boundary shifts remains open.

